Z||000005||JSocha||11-05-2001||09:19 AM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.junkbusters.com" TARGET=_blank>JUNKBUSTERS</A>.   They have some good guidelines on SPAM EMAIL and how to avoid this junk, etc., along with junk mail and telemarketing callers.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good luck...I'm fighting the same battle here at work on our standard sales email account as well as home where I get junk email from foreign countries. I don't even speak Spanish or whatever it is in.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||11-05-2001||10:01 AM||||Solution:  don't give out your email address.  If you have AOL... sorry, you're screwed.<P>Sign up an email account with Hotmail or something to use for when programs require an email address, or if you want to sign up for mailing lists ect.  <B>Never</B> just put your regular email down for things on the internet.  Notice, I don't even use my real email on this forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||11-05-2001||10:38 AM||||easiest way it to close that email account and open another one, dont give it out||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||11-05-2001||11:02 AM||||How about telemarketers?<BR>Every day for over two weeks, I have been receiving an automated phone call. I'm never home to get the call, and all I hear on my voicemail message is the last four digits and the hours I can reach this person. If I could get the complete phone number, I'd call and have a friendly conversation with this person. I've got caller ID, and it says Out of Area.<BR>I'm just really sick of this, and I can't wait to get the phone number!||||reg||5
Z||000009||JSocha||11-05-2001||11:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>How about telemarketers?<BR>I'm just really sick of this, and I can't wait to get the phone number!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Get "TeleZapper" for $49.99.  <P>What it does is when you or your answering machine picks up, it sends back a "disconnected" tone to the telemarkerters computer system which tells there system the number is no longer in service (even though it is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) but there systems don't know that.<P>You can pick them up at any Radio Shack, Wal Mart, KMart (sorry Roger  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), etc. or on the internet.<P>Its made by Private Technologies, Inc.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tigger||11-05-2001||12:26 PM||||Anyone using a hotmail account, look into using the custom filters to filter out spam.  I did here a week ago and It helps a lot.<P>I tried blocking spam using the block sender method.  That worked for about month or so till I hit the 250 sender limit!<P>Anyway, with the filter you add keywords so when they are used in the subject line it will direct the spam into a junk mail folder.  The folder is automatically cleaned out about every 14 days.  You can look at it to make sure a message didn't accidently get filtered in there and you can dump the folder anytime.<P>Now everytime I get a spam I look at the subject line, pick a keyword they used that nobody will likely put in the subject line in an email to you.  I have about 25 seperate keyword filters already, most are obvious, adult words, debt, refinance, dating, mortgage, viagra, you get the point.<P>I've recieved about 45 spam messages since halloween.  31 of those are sitting in my junk mail folder awaiting for the mystic spam portal of death.<P>Muahahaha!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||11-05-2001||03:22 PM||||ur rite, i use hotmail for my primary mail. it does a great job. Not hardly one spam/porn mail gets thru. all i have to do is click for bulk mail and it deletes them all at one click, never even have to look at one. As an extra benefit, hotmail also scans all out in incoming mail for viruses for free.||||reg||1
Z||000012||terryk||11-05-2001||05:50 PM||||Interesting since Hotmail is one of the major sources of spam.||||reg||1
Z||000013||maryjane||11-05-2001||08:58 PM||||I use earthlink--Not the greatest, but their 'spaminator' must work, never have I received any spam of any kind.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cooter||11-05-2001||11:38 PM||||I just set the mail preferances in AOL to reject mail from the domains where I kept getting the spam from- mostly uu.net, excite.com, cw.net, and globix.com<BR>Since then, my crap mail has gone to only about 3-5 per day.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Flamberge||11-06-2001||12:45 AM||||Thanks all... one of the ideas I have heard is to send an email to "abuse@****.***" (whatever the ISP is of the spammer) since most of the time the ISP doesn't know it is going on, or something. I did this when I got a porn email from a hotmail account, and it took two emails to them (abuse@) but that sender never sent me another one. <P>I am also thinking about replying to the spam with "mailer deamons," which might (or might not) make them think I am a dead link.<P>Ultimately I think I am simply going to change my home email addy.<P>Another thing I do (since I have unlimited email addresses through my homepage server) is whenever I sign up for something (like Quicktime 5) I use what I downloaded as the prefix of the email. "QT5@*****.***" so that when I get spammed from that address, I know it was Apple who sold my info.<P>Any other ideas? (thanks all!!)<P><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
